// Rule: [T1059.001][T1105] Exvicy - Clickfix Invokescript Download
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.001, T1105
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Hunts for the source-observed PowerShell pattern that downloads script text with irm and executes it in memory through ExecutionContext.InvokeCommand.InvokeScript.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for clickfix invokescript download using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: successful exploitation, malicious ownership, downstream impact, campaign attribution or complete compromise without corroborating evidence.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Exvicy ClickFix PowerShell download-and-InvokeScript
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Status: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceProcessEvents
// A match does not prove ClickFix delivery, Exvicy attribution, malicious content, or successful execution.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName in~ ("powershell.exe", "pwsh.exe")
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "$ExecutionContext.InvokeCommand.InvokeScript"
| where ProcessCommandLine has "irm"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountName, AccountUpn,
          FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          ProcessUniqueId, InitiatingProcessUniqueId, ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
